# --- F42. The renames ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# The edits were one line each. The names were the harder half.
#
#   test_WBH_1_the_app_declares_exactly_the_three_spec_routes
#     -> test_WBH_1_the_app_declares_exactly_the_spec_routes
#
# The count came out of the name. It was wrong within one checkpoint of being
# written and would have been wrong again at five; the assertion still pins the
# set exactly, which is the property worth having, and the docstring carries the
# current number where a stale one costs nothing.
#
#   test_VIW_6_the_mount_does_not_widen_the_api_surface
#     -> test_VIW_6_the_chart_mount_adds_no_route_to_the_api_surface
#
# This one read as though it were about the route count. It is not: it is about
# a `StaticFiles` mount being a sub-application rather than a route, so the
# charts could be served without the fourth route CP14 rejected. The route set
# is the backdrop; the mount's absence from it is the claim.
#
# A test name that lies is the thing this project is about. WBH-1's said three
# while the suite was green at four for the length of one checkpoint — it was
# only ever going to be caught by the assertion underneath it, which is the
# wrong way round.

# --- F43. The preset correction ----------------------------------------------
#
# SPEC A151, and PLAN under CP18.
#
# Two of screen 4's three presets were built on `time_shiftable`, whose viable
# set under §9 is {do_nothing, retry}. G1 blocks contacts. G6 suppresses
# contacts. Neither had a contact to act on, so both screens rendered a correct
# table that demonstrated nothing — no wrong number, no error, nothing to notice
# unless you already knew what the gate was supposed to do.
#
# Both moved to `do_not_honour`. `ambiguous` is the only class carrying a retry
# and a message at once, which is what makes "the gate stopped the message and
# left the retry running" visible at all.
#
# The anchor moved with them: 00:30 UTC put tick 0 at 06:00 IST, outside G1's
# window, so an untouched form's first Decide met a contact blocked by the
# clock. 04:30 UTC is 10:00 IST at tick 0 and 02:00 IST at tick 16.
#
# Worth the amendment because it is SF-shaped: silent, self-consistent, and on
# the one surface a judge was going to look at.
